cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Public Safety Statistics Tutorials: Time Series and Causal Inference"
message: "If you use these materials, please cite them as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Yin
    email: yin.zhang@wsu.edu
    affiliation: "Center for Interdisciplinary Statistical Education and Research (CISER), Washington State University"
abstract: >-
  A tutorial series teaching time series analysis and causal inference to
  public safety audiences, from readers with no statistics background through
  agency data analysts and early career researchers. Every example uses a
  synthetic dataset modeled on the Washington Data Exchange for Public Safety
  (WADEPS), with known patterns built in so that each method can be checked
  against the answer it is supposed to find.
keywords:
  - public safety
  - law enforcement data
  - time series analysis
  - causal inference
  - statistical education
  - WADEPS
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
